{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "2CO",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we know that if our earthly house of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tabernacle were dissolved, we have a building of God, a house not made with hands, eternal in the heavens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in this we groan, earnestly desiring to be clothed with our house which is from heaven:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If so be that being clothed we shall not be found naked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we that are in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tabernacle do groan, being burdened: not because we would be unclothed, but clothed, that mortality might be swallowed up in life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now he that hath wrought us for this same thing ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God, who also hath given to us the earnest of the Spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "we are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " always confident, knowing that, while we are at home in the body, we are absent from the Lord:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For we walk by faith, not by sight:)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We are confident, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I say",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and willing rather to be absent from the body, and to be present with the Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore we labor, that, whether present or absent, we may be accepted by him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we must all appear before the judgment-seat of Christ; that every one may receive the things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "done",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " body, according to what he hath done, whether good or bad.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowing therefore the terror of the Lord, we persuade men; but we are made manifest to God; and I trust also are made manifest in your consciences.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we commend not ourselves again to you, but give you occasion to glory on our behalf, that ye may have somewhat to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "answer",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " them who glory in appearance, and not in heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For whether we are beside ourselves, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to God: or whether we are sober, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for your cause.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the love of Christ constraineth us; because we thus judge, that if one died for all, then were all dead:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he died for all, that they who live should not henceforth live to themselves, but to him who died for them, and rose again.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore henceforth we know no man according to the flesh: though indeed we have known Christ according to the flesh, yet now henceforth we know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore, if any man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Christ, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a new creature: old things have passed away; behold, all things have become new.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from God, who hath reconciled us to himself by Jesus Christ, and hath given to us the ministry of reconciliation;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To wit, that God was in Christ, reconciling the world to himself, not imputing their trespasses to them; and hath committed to us the word of reconciliation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now then we are embassadors for Christ, as though God did beseech ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "you",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by us: we pray ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "you",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Christ's stead, be ye reconciled to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.5.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.5.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he hath made him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sin for us, who knew no sin; that we might be made the righteousness of God in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
